=== email subject
[Action needed by 12 Oct 2026] 3 actively exploited flaws in your products
=== email body
Patchtacio found 3 known exploited vulnerabilities (CISA KEV) that affect products on your list. Attackers are already using all of them. Start with the earliest deadline.
Patchtacio matched them by product name and has not checked whether your versions are affected.

New:
1. [Action needed by 12 Oct 2026] Fortinet FortiOS: actively exploited flaw (CVE-2026-24858)
   Fortinet Multiple Products Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel Vulnerability. Added to CISA's list 28 Sep 2026.
   What to do: check the vendor advisory for the fixed version: https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-060
   If you cannot update yet, follow CISA's required action: "Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, follow applicable BOD 22-01 guidance for cloud services, or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable."
   Details: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24858
2. [Action needed now] Microsoft Exchange Server: actively exploited flaw (CVE-2023-21529)
   Microsoft Exchange Server Deserialization of Untrusted Data Vulnerability. Added to CISA's list 13 Apr 2026. Linked to ransomware campaigns.
   What to do: check the vendor advisory for the fixed version: https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2023-21529
   If you cannot update yet, follow CISA's required action: "Apply mitigations per vendor instructions or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable."
   Details: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-21529

Reminders (nobody has acknowledged these yet):
1. [Reminder: deadline passed 11 Apr 2025] Ivanti Connect Secure: actively exploited flaw (CVE-2025-22457)
   Ivanti Connect Secure, Policy Secure, and ZTA Gateways Stack-Based Buffer Overflow Vulnerability. Added to CISA's list 4 Apr 2025.
   What to do: check the vendor's security advisory for CVE-2025-22457 to find the fixed version.
   Details: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-22457

For each entry, CISA's deadline is the one it set for US government agencies. Use it as a guide to how urgent each one is.

--
When you have dealt with one, run: patchtacio ack <CVE ID>, for example: patchtacio ack CVE-2026-24858
Patchtacio then stops reminding you about it.
You get this alert because Microsoft Exchange Server (on-premises), Fortinet FortiOS (FortiGate firewalls) and Ivanti Connect Secure (formerly Pulse Connect Secure VPN) are on your Patchtacio product list.
