=== web UI cards
# [Action needed now] Microsoft Exchange Server: actively exploited flaw (CVE-2023-21529)
affected: Microsoft Exchange Server (on-premises)
caveat: Patchtacio matched this by product name and has not checked whether your version is affected.
why: Attackers are already using this flaw: Microsoft Exchange Server Deserialization of Untrusted Data Vulnerability (CVE-2023-21529). CISA added it to its list of exploited vulnerabilities on 13 Apr 2026. Linked to ransomware campaigns.
What to do:
  1. Update: check the vendor advisory for the fixed version: https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2023-21529
  2. If you cannot update yet, follow CISA's required action: "Apply mitigations per vendor instructions or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable."
  3. If neither is possible, disconnect it or restrict who can reach it until you can update.
deadline: CISA's deadline for US government agencies, 27 Apr 2026, has passed: act as soon as you can.
link: Vendor advisory: https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2023-21529
link: CISA KEV entry: https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog?search_api_fulltext=CVE-2023-21529
link: NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-21529
# [Action needed by 12 Oct 2026] Fortinet FortiOS: actively exploited flaw (CVE-2026-24858)
affected: Fortinet FortiOS (FortiGate firewalls), version 7.4.2 (your note: edge firewall, main office)
caveat: Patchtacio matched this by product name and has not checked whether your version is affected.
why: Attackers are already using this flaw: Fortinet Multiple Products Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel Vulnerability (CVE-2026-24858). CISA added it to its list of exploited vulnerabilities on 28 Sep 2026.
why: Fortinet FortiOS, FortiManager and FortiAnalyzer contain an authentication bypass that may allow an attacker with a FortiCloud account to log into other devices.
What to do by 12 Oct 2026:
  1. Update: check the vendor advisory for the fixed version: https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-060
  2. If you cannot update yet, follow CISA's required action: "Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, follow applicable BOD 22-01 guidance for cloud services, or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable."
  3. If neither is possible, disconnect it or restrict who can reach it until you can update.
deadline: CISA set 12 Oct 2026 as the deadline for US government agencies. Use it as a guide to how urgent this is.
link: Vendor advisory: https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-060
link: CISA KEV entry: https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog?search_api_fulltext=CVE-2026-24858
link: NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24858
# [Reminder: deadline passed 11 Apr 2025] Ivanti Connect Secure: actively exploited flaw (CVE-2025-22457)
affected: Ivanti Connect Secure (formerly Pulse Connect Secure VPN)
caveat: Patchtacio matched this by product name and has not checked whether your version is affected.
why: Attackers are already using this flaw: Ivanti Connect Secure, Policy Secure, and ZTA Gateways Stack-Based Buffer Overflow Vulnerability (CVE-2025-22457). CISA added it to its list of exploited vulnerabilities on 4 Apr 2025.
What to do:
  1. Update: check the vendor's security advisory for CVE-2025-22457 to find the fixed version.
  2. If you cannot update yet, apply the vendor's mitigations.
  3. If neither is possible, disconnect it or restrict who can reach it until you can update.
deadline: CISA's deadline for US government agencies, 11 Apr 2025, has passed: act as soon as you can.
link: CISA KEV entry: https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog?search_api_fulltext=CVE-2025-22457
link: NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-22457
